<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      DO NOT add default_web_client_id here.

      This file used to hard-code it as
        331867448304-saipigd6cpsquunjvv9r88cl3lidc127.apps.googleusercontent.com
      which belongs to a DIFFERENT Google Cloud project than this app's
      (378436113717). The com.google.gms.google-services Gradle plugin
      generates default_web_client_id from android/app/google-services.json,
      and a hand-written copy in src/main/res overrides that generated value —
      so Android resolved the wrong project's client id no matter what
      google-services.json said. That was one of the reasons Google sign-in
      failed with DEVELOPER_ERROR (code 10).

      The web client id now lives in exactly two places, and they must match:
        - android/app/google-services.json  (client_type 3, written by Firebase)
        - serverClientId in lib/features/auth/viewmodels/auth_viewmodel.dart
      Change it in Firebase, re-download google-services.json, and update the
      Dart constant. Never reintroduce it as a resource here.
    -->
</resources>
